## Architecture rules

- **Routes** never import repositories directly. Always go through a service.
- **Services** raise domain exceptions (`NotFoundError`, `AlreadyExistsError`) — never return `None` for "not found".
- **Repositories** use `db.flush()` + `db.refresh()`, NEVER `db.commit()` (session auto-commits in `get_db_session`).
- **Pydantic schemas:** separate `*Create`, `*Update`, `*Read`, `*List` per operation.
- **Migrations:** one Alembic revision per logical change; never edit a merged migration.

See `docs/en/guides/architecture.md` for the full layered architecture rules.
{%- if enable_precommit %}

## Pre-commit

Configured via `.pre-commit-config.yaml`. Install once:

```bash
uv run pre-commit install
```

Will run ruff + (frontend lint if present) on every commit. Bypass with `--no-verify` only when fixing a hook bug.
{%- endif %}

## Container images

The base images of the Dockerfiles, the Compose files and the CI are pinned by tag: the
generator has no registry access to read their digests. A tag can be moved to other content; a
digest (`image:tag@sha256:...`) cannot.
{%- if use_gitlab_ci %}

Renovate (`renovate.json`, preset `docker:pinDigests`) adds the digests in its first merge
requests and keeps tag and digest current afterwards. Review and merge them; no manual step.
{%- else %}

Dependabot (`.github/dependabot.yml`) keeps a digest current only once it is present. Pin
every image once, from a machine with registry access:

```bash
# The digest of the multi-platform index: the value to pin.
docker buildx imagetools inspect postgres:16-alpine | grep -m1 '^Digest:'
```

Write it after the tag wherever the image appears (`grep -rn "postgres:16-alpine" .`), for
example `postgres:16-alpine@sha256:<digest>`, and keep the tag: Dependabot reads it to propose
the next version and updates tag and digest together. Images built by this project
(`{{ project_slug }}_backend`) are not pinned. Dependabot reads the Dockerfiles and the Compose
files; the service images of `.github/workflows/ci.yml` are updated by hand, digest included,
when their tag changes.
{%- endif %}

## Pull-request checklist

- [ ] `uv run ruff check . && uv run ruff format --check .` clean
{%- if use_frontend %}
- [ ] `cd frontend && bunx tsc --noEmit` clean
{%- endif %}
{%- if enable_pytest %}
- [ ] Tests added for new code paths; `uv run pytest` green
{%- endif %}
- [ ] If schema changed: alembic migration committed (`uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "..."`)
- [ ] Updated `ENV_VARS.md` if new env vars added
- [ ] Updated `CHANGELOG.md` (if applicable)
